.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt PRINTENV 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm printenv
.Nd print the process environment
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no operands, print sorted
.Ql KEY=VALUE
entries, one per line.
Otherwise print each named value in operand order; unset or invalid names
produce no value and set status 1.
There are no options: dash-leading words are variable names.
An ordinary SSH session has an empty environment.
This command cannot modify its parent shell or grant authority through
environment variables.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 if all requested values exist, or the full environment was printed;
1 if any requested value is unavailable.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printenv
printenv HOME
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr absd-sh 1 ,
.Xr process 7
